  "title": "osf review run: lens-driven agent review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds `osf review run`, a new review pipeline that selects review lenses for a change, assembles a redacted context prompt, runs coding-agent harnesses from a shipped roster over each lens, verifies every quoted finding against the real files, reduces the answers to a per-lens and whole-review verdict, and journals each answer and the decision. Alongside it, the change adds a secret-shape scan rule, suppression-marker ownership so a checker only reports its own unused markers, and a base-branch GitHub workflow that runs the review with the pull request's tree mounted read-only as data.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
